## Task

You are a professional software architect. Based on the following requirements document, identify the core business entities described in the system, and generate a simple architecture diagram that represents each entity as a module in the system using Mermaid syntax.

## Method
1. Read the requirements document carefully and extract all major business entities (e.g., Student, Teacher, Course, etc.). Don't split too much, focus on high-level entities only;
2. For each entity, define a module named after the entity using PascalCase, and connect it to the root system node;
3. Use Mermaid's graph TD syntax;
4. Do not include any relationships or interactions between modules — only a flat module breakdown.

## Constraints
- Each module corresponds to a single core business entity;
- Use PascalCase for module names (e.g., StudentModule, CourseModule);
- Keep the structure simple and clear;
- All modules must be connected directly to the main system node;
- Do not include technical, functional, or cross-cutting modules like Auth, Notification, or Report;
- Return only the Mermaid diagram in a Markdown code block with no extra explanation.

## Requirements Document

```markdown
${product_requirement}
```

## Output example
```mermaid
graph TD
    StudentManageSystem --> StudentModule
    StudentManageSystem --> TeacherModule
    StudentManageSystem --> CourseModule
    StudentManageSystem --> EnrollmentModule
    StudentManageSystem --> GradeModule

```